# November 28, 2026: state hospitals and asylums of Ohio, a batch of the themed pass on historic state hospitals.
# Already on the map and left alone: the Southern Ohio Lunatic Asylum (Dayton State Hospital) and the Toledo State
# Hospital Old Cemetery. Toledo's hospital itself was razed in the early 1990s, so its second burial ground, the New
# Cemetery with its marker, stands in for it here.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia (Athens Lunatic Asylum, Athens State Hospital Cow Barn, Columbus State
# Hospital, Columbus Developmental Center, Allen-Oakwood Correctional Institution, Pickaway Correctional Institution);
# the Park Service's National Register records for the Athens State Hospital (80002936) and the Gallipolis water towers
# (78002069); the Register's cover document "Federal and State Correctional Institutions in Ohio" (2006, amended
# 2019-2021) for Lima and Orient; SAH Archipedia; KirkbrideBuildings.com; Ohio State University Libraries' medical
# heritage blog; WOSU; the Encyclopedia of Cleveland History; Cleveland Historical; us-data.org; Asylum Projects;
# the Galbreath-Hartley-Mahan (Packard) pages at ghmchs.org; HMdb's copies of three Ohio markers; TrailLink; the
# University of Toledo's library and news pages; and the own pages of the Kennedy Museum of Art and the Dairy Barn.
# Pins: OpenStreetMap points, the ArcGIS geocoder, a Wikipedia coordinate and marker positions, each looked at on
# the aerial (see PIN_NOTES).
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
